{"experiment_id":"EXP-015","date":"2026-09-11","description":"Phase 20 fix #5: hybrid (dense+BM25 via RRF k=10) vs dense-only retrieval","embedding_model":"sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2","chunk_size":256,"chunk_overlap":32,"retrieval_top_k":5,"reranking_enabled":false,"final_context_size":5,"generation_model":null,"retrieval_metrics":{"hit_rate":0.9411764705882353,"mrr":0.7191176470588235,"precision_at_k":0.3294117647058824,"recall_at_k":0.2679699657640834,"ndcg_at_k":0.39831515380379334},"generation_metrics":{},"latency_seconds":null,"notes":"Hybrid beat dense-only (EXP-004/007, same fixed config) on every metric (hit_rate 0.82->0.94, mrr 0.60->0.72, ndcg 0.30->0.40). RRF k=10, not the commonly-cited k=60, which was found to bury a real single-source top match (a MOCOnet query where BM25 alone ranked correctly at #1) once candidates exceeded k. Promoted to the API/scripts default based on this result."}
